Because these files contain their own `setup()` and `loop()` functions, they cannot be compiled alongside the main application. To run a specific hardware test:

1. Copy the contents of the desired test file (e.g., `MQ2.cpp`).
2. Paste it into your primary `src/main.cpp`, temporarily overwriting your main application logic.
3. Build and upload to the ESP32 via PlatformIO. 
4. Monitor the serial output at `115200` baud to verify the hardware behavior.